    {
      "id": "a15",
      "status": "partially_cited",
      "good": false,
      "answer": "LLM inference is both cheaper and faster than human labelers.  \n- **Cost**: Human labeling cost about \\$2,250, which is roughly 100 × higher than the cost of GPT‑4 inference [3].  \n- **Speed**: Human labelers required about 112 hours (≈6,720 minutes) to annotate the data, whereas GPT‑4 completed the same task in about 27.5 minutes, giving a speed‑up of roughly 244 × [4]."
    },
